# Cloudflare Pages (and Netlify) headers.
# Always revalidate the service worker and app shell so a new deploy is picked
# up. The cache-first SW (sw.js) serves these from Cache Storage between deploys,
# so no-cache costs ~nothing in bandwidth — it only ensures the install-time
# precache and any cache miss fetch the CURRENT deploy's files, not a stale CDN
# copy. Without this, a long edge/browser cache on the non-hashed asset names
# could hide a deploy from the SW.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
